#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087464 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19d1448c-d5fd-5615-b657-ff4d66867834" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "67da2ffa-b472-5084-985c-dde4cd2df661" :question/math-academy-id "e-5219" :question/problem "What is the equation of the ellipse given below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/assets/57ec3c089f80e2d35d9b83f6791eefca9b452d933f82209ed434d35d77b78788.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{{a}^2}+\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{{b}^2}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(1,-1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=5,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087467 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "e01914e2-b4f0-52b5-baf1-8b7fa5da3f18" :question/math-academy-id "e-5222" :question/problem "What is the equation of the ellipse given below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/assets/b6eb2c0222181eaa4eb2a1c232fdf2eee905ab0e0a8a9c2284911ab8dd26cade.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{{a}^2}+\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{{b}^2}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-1,-3),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087468 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "10dda4fa-e047-53f4-a20a-b881e14f3e2a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5223" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\dfrac{(x-2)^2}{25} + \\dfrac{(y+2)^2}{16} = 1,$ find its center, and the lengths of its major and minor axes." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{{a}^2}+\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{{b}^2}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=2$ and $k=-2,$ so the center is located at $(2,-2).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have $a^2=25$ and $b^2=16.$\n\n- Since $a^2=25,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{25} = 5.$\n\n- Since $b^2=16,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{16} = 4.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=5,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=4.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a = 2\\cdot5 = 10,$ and the minor axis has length $2b = 2\\cdot4 = 8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b88c73f5-8496-543d-8919-1a8e540e5a8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299761} {:answer/id #uuid "11b714a6-cb98-567e-a257-6690859bf3fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{49}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{81}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299762} {:answer/id #uuid "e515b34b-ecba-50ff-a873-02ab4401a509" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299763} {:answer/id #uuid "a1c16aed-2edc-5e00-b274-23c7dc32dc76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299764} {:answer/id #uuid "334ad9bb-777e-5df5-b10c-62b1eb9a3532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1c16aed-2edc-5e00-b274-23c7dc32dc76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299764} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c985307-3687-52c6-bad4-e0e2a9734395" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "160e6bfa-97cf-5c52-982c-614ccb081e05" :question/math-academy-id "q-115293" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/assets/9699c059d44d63cac608c76e130381139973a9d1579b4703801ec9b99f4e5e6e.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(4,5),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=3,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282091 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d84c2b7-7e87-5003-a0ae-cf907011148a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282093} {:answer/id #uuid "897f2f6b-955d-5a90-b368-aafbe23fc778" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282094} {:answer/id #uuid "238b4156-fe38-512b-8174-689e062953d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282095} {:answer/id #uuid "6d1de455-fa3c-55bb-9b6a-8ec1e3f8b163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282096} {:answer/id #uuid "4662b591-a4d4-5680-8213-224d41f4d23e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4662b591-a4d4-5680-8213-224d41f4d23e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282097} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb73f107-6494-54b1-8438-bfd8864c7ff9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282092}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eb7c4e5a-23fb-5e2d-b89b-6f04ed6e4095" :question/math-academy-id "q-115310" :question/problem "What is the center of the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{25}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=0$ and $k=-4,$ so the center is located at $(0,-4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "936a69db-4967-5baf-ad89-064aaeb39719" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084892} {:answer/id #uuid "f959d3f3-8a75-53a4-9392-4649a0af59e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084893} {:answer/id #uuid "fc9c6bea-c288-5a19-b7f7-b78194580dc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084894} {:answer/id #uuid "5500795a-23bf-571d-b3ea-99e83b3e11b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084895} {:answer/id #uuid "6a0edcf6-fcf1-573c-9e18-f0bb648336c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc9c6bea-c288-5a19-b7f7-b78194580dc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084894} :answer-field/id #uuid "42ddd405-a175-5967-9ce7-bfbf2b649fe1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ec2c80f9-6d60-5c98-a90e-0bf456ed1faa" :question/math-academy-id "q-16461" :question/problem "What is the center of the ellipse $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=1$ and $k=-2,$ so the center is located at $(1,-2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087981 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19d1448c-d5fd-5615-b657-ff4d66867834" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e811d5f7-fdcf-508d-a255-b0269c7d721e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 3)^{2} + ((y - 1)^{2})/(25) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084898} {:answer/id #uuid "eae71074-b5dc-52b2-a28f-f70d6a514ac5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x - 3)^{2})/(25) + (y + 1)^{2} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084899} {:answer/id #uuid "2c2e783d-33d4-5dfa-88aa-26de8a5e351b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x - 3)^{2})/(25) + ((y + 1)^{2})/(4) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084900} {:answer/id #uuid "603bfca7-e359-504c-b0b8-af447c5f8b8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 3)^{2} + ((y + 1)^{2})/(25) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084901} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0d61bb-3de8-50c1-92b8-c86a0098aacc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x + 3)^{2})/(25) + (y - 1)^{2} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eae71074-b5dc-52b2-a28f-f70d6a514ac5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x - 3)^{2})/(25) + (y + 1)^{2} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084899} :answer-field/id #uuid "b335553e-1f6e-5975-937c-02a13094fc5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bf0d584b-d17a-5da7-8790-1a7a4cd3e967" :question/math-academy-id "q-16555" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/assets/92a107b34d3ed8c422b35dc33eec5f54a47bc0db054f5a6c61b390d996d8bec4.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(3,-1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=5,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=1.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{25}+(y+1)^{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267552 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d972cb7-f674-5723-919a-f6d3dc0421ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^2}{4}+\\frac{(y+3)^2}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d972cb7-f674-5723-919a-f6d3dc0421ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^2}{4}+\\frac{(y+3)^2}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267554} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed274ac7-35bf-5a13-8527-60067f477907" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267553}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "01c8b954-6543-5e80-b060-0261735b6399" :question/math-academy-id "q-278254" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/assets/65a76a438b3459a92db0e00b0c9bd281b8a9c58fa68afd2d8e6468a1d99b1cf9.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-1,-3),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299766 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19d1448c-d5fd-5615-b657-ff4d66867834" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cd7b387-e6d2-578f-81a1-a879484dc6f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^2}{25}+\\frac{(y+1)^2}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cd7b387-e6d2-578f-81a1-a879484dc6f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^2}{25}+\\frac{(y+1)^2}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299768} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bd2e3eb-83eb-59a2-85a4-856b2e1e6287" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e37e5c99-f4e7-535a-b47e-79ad46d4f44d" :question/math-academy-id "q-278255" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/assets/4c95243ea94951012ec14c6f16b4276a591c10c22798efc82f73bcd9d45e65ae.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-4,-1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=5,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-4))^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299769 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22deb66e-5e78-5951-be4f-1ae2ffda1c5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-6)^2}{9}+\\frac{y^2}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299771} {:answer/id #uuid "98f379a7-0954-5831-9002-4189e49954cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-6)^2}{36}+\\frac{y^2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22deb66e-5e78-5951-be4f-1ae2ffda1c5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-6)^2}{9}+\\frac{y^2}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299771} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5013c2c-4868-59d0-a27b-a2c9a4548036" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ce98f2e0-6ed9-52bc-9c0e-fcc399b98190" :question/math-academy-id "q-278395" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/assets/33adaa159f0926038c6b04a750b6a61b8a18e0fe2df9c6c3c581c139e27b2c95.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(6,0),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=3,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-0)^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299773 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58fa4f7e-e9fc-51fe-ade5-af17c2a43bfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{4}+\\frac{(y+5)^2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299775} {:answer/id #uuid "cfa01e02-6c59-5363-9f3d-27a697e45447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{4}+\\frac{(y-5)^2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfa01e02-6c59-5363-9f3d-27a697e45447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{4}+\\frac{(y-5)^2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299776} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1fe4127-c821-51ee-8e22-dec017dc030f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "961e5475-3c5e-59e1-82c7-c4526ff0e464" :question/math-academy-id "q-278398" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/assets/441ee336bc10f5787a5956a6c118cde9faaa0485c3c2f8a6adb9dd93903b3972.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(0,5),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-0)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282102 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9797b665-acfe-5ef3-ab9d-e451919b916e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282104} {:answer/id #uuid "b3b18822-8955-5d83-a983-ce01e53b13ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9797b665-acfe-5ef3-ab9d-e451919b916e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282104} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbde829e-e840-53ab-8dd2-2f44399375ff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282103} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "382ed5a1-6a4a-5d26-a33d-4491ffb005ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "382ed5a1-6a4a-5d26-a33d-4491ffb005ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282106} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3349205-1811-5815-9329-dbfa5f8bc11b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1d364c20-40e0-58aa-a4d5-2b6f9f2f6ac4" :question/math-academy-id "q-278401" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{49}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{7}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=6$ and $k=-5,$ so the center is located at $(6,-5).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=49$ and ${b}^{2}=7.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=49,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=7,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{7}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\sqrt{7}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{7}=2\\sqrt{7}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97a56b89-7939-55e5-aa7f-0de277930e6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97a56b89-7939-55e5-aa7f-0de277930e6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267561} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0a3e32c-7502-5d12-a165-e06a2e52dcdd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267560} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "375397a9-b308-5964-af77-9cc319b096b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "375397a9-b308-5964-af77-9cc319b096b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267563} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d3002bc-bbe1-5c58-b61e-5c7eeded7b0d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267562}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b74a983b-5b3e-5c81-aeef-49a17e380aae" :question/math-academy-id "q-278402" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x+7)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{11}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=-7$ and $k=-5,$ so the center is located at $(-7,-5).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=3$ and ${b}^{2}=11.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=3,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=11,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{11}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=\\sqrt{11},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{11}=2\\sqrt{11},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{3}=2\\sqrt{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299778 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43ed3421-e059-50da-9caa-59c6b50de0bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43ed3421-e059-50da-9caa-59c6b50de0bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299780} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7c78f1b-3001-57b5-ab6d-8c80df2b0202" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299779} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2af3838-00ce-50ba-96be-b1b9739463bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2af3838-00ce-50ba-96be-b1b9739463bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299782} :answer-field/id #uuid "eeea0247-4051-5ee8-94d0-a5633c07c08d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299781}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96ae2185-6307-5de4-8916-3673bdc7e5d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-278403" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{15}+\\frac{(y-6)^{2}}{49}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=1$ and $k=6,$ so the center is located at $(1,6).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=15$ and ${b}^{2}=49.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=15,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{15}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=49,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{15}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{15}=2\\sqrt{15}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299783 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19d1448c-d5fd-5615-b657-ff4d66867834" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "772905d0-0ab1-5edc-9fe6-fbcc576f8010" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^2}{4}+(y+2)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "772905d0-0ab1-5edc-9fe6-fbcc576f8010" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^2}{4}+(y+2)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299785} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ca1a81d-904d-56a4-8f59-f24e3dac94ba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "24816f3b-1b1c-56fc-b9f4-7f4fca50b6f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-278477" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/assets/fb178149bac4d1fcfd0690b7005f263c3647488ac86ed70f1143540e23e04b6e.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(2,-2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=1.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+(y+2)^{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299786 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19d1448c-d5fd-5615-b657-ff4d66867834" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3272340d-0b80-5895-a2b2-849e5f936a9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{25}+\\frac{(y+2)^2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299788} {:answer/id #uuid "3a95d8b7-c161-5caf-84d9-67bce1a0e9d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{25}+\\frac{(y-2)^2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3272340d-0b80-5895-a2b2-849e5f936a9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{25}+\\frac{(y+2)^2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299788} :answer-field/id #uuid "a47bc24e-0206-55c2-8541-67320c54da03" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "575091ca-c066-5dc8-bc9e-438154e0aabb" :question/math-academy-id "q-278482" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/assets/19611e305d49d136f0a79189773b712243ec12f957fe16efca22ec2812393bd8.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(0,-2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=5,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-0)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299790 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19d1448c-d5fd-5615-b657-ff4d66867834" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb53ebc2-9fbf-51e9-858c-dd41f050ebe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299792} {:answer/id #uuid "25a68b5e-271f-555d-b7fc-9618213254a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299793} {:answer/id #uuid "a747cd23-5c0c-593a-80d5-47d5e7169653" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299794} {:answer/id #uuid "53da4063-5a70-51da-95d8-06ba9cd460ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299795} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb25a14-d109-5c83-bfa2-3edca02519b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdb25a14-d109-5c83-bfa2-3edca02519b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299796} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e322686-ef32-59ea-96c4-ebc5020e3a8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "548de5f2-ff25-5fbe-ae9c-9d2cdd48470d" :question/math-academy-id "q-72249" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/assets/a0b2f29f1b6c99163f51b1c6a1a278a7796730148ec45952dd222161f3b3d762.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(3,-4),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=3,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-4))^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088273 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6b6a114-fcf4-59dc-8717-07a8f96bfbec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x + 1)^{2})/(4) + ((y - 3)^{2})/(16) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086570} {:answer/id #uuid "e09415b9-b0b6-5162-91db-605f6f448c04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x - 3)^{2})/(8) + ((y + 1)^{2})/(2) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086571} {:answer/id #uuid "2088c170-af4d-5902-9e39-24d71284d87b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x + 3)^{2})/(4) + ((y - 1)^{2})/(16) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086572} {:answer/id #uuid "5dd41287-65a2-5acf-8910-60f0222f18de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x + 3)^{2})/(2) + ((y - 1)^{2})/(8) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086573} {:answer/id #uuid "786d85f2-ff1e-56c8-92ff-879e5ac52192" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x - 3)^{2})/(4) + ((y + 1)^{2})/(16) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "786d85f2-ff1e-56c8-92ff-879e5ac52192" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x - 3)^{2})/(4) + ((y + 1)^{2})/(16) = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086574} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa33e9aa-8875-5c99-9a88-261fa19140ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "573849bd-9036-5460-9507-bc3e024db188" :question/math-academy-id "q-7627" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038597/assets/2ab9745cb9d157e566c101a6ca79514017903fa57eaf8725c846afd272c74f93.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(3,-1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
